{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings","id":1153125,"title":"Speculating on Titan Callings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-26T05:27:27-07:00","id":1153125,"title":"Speculating on Titan Callings","content":"Neall revealed on the Ask thread that Titans will have distinct Callings from Gods. Anyone want to join me in some idle speculation about what the roles of Titans in Fate might be?<br /> <br /> - Adversary: a Titan locked in some form of all consuming metaphysical conflict with a God, which it is defined by. Apep to Re is an obvious example<br /> <br /> - Beast: Monstrous and beastial Titans<br /> <br /> - Creator, as the God Calling; disproportionately these are \u201cGreat Mother\u201d Titans, but you get some outliers like Prometheus too. All Titan Creators have the Fecundity Virtue<br /> <br /> - Embodiments: Titans who continue to serve their function as the pure incarnation of a given Purview in a God ruled cosmology. Helios and Selene are obvious examples. All Embodiments have the Submission Virtue.<br /> <br /> - Entropic: a Titan who embodies the decline of the world, serving to wear it down, think Nidhogg, though Ran with her ever growing host of the drowned is also a good fit. All Entropics have the Rapacity Virtue.<br /> <br /> - Humanist: No Titan has the capacity to truly conceive of the world in human terms the way gods can, but some do care, even if it\u2019s an abstract way through the filter of their dominant Purview. Rare others come closer to understanding the world through a human lens because they were humans who achieved apotheosis before being consumed by their Purview. All humanists have 1 Pantheon Virtue and 1 Titan Virtue, whether they\u2019re aligned with the Gods or not.<br /> <br /> - Sessile: Titans who express their purview passively, but with great metaphysical weight often drawing on other agents to serve them, and being unmovable in their natures. Crom Cruach fits this mold, as does Ao Guang who just wants Nezha and Sun Wukong to leave him the fuck alone!<br /> <br /> - Uncrowned: No Titans rule over Pantheons anymore, but once it was common. Those former rulers whose continued existence now represents the old order the gods conquered have this Calling. All Uncrowned have the Dominance Virtue<br /> <br /> - Unifier: Cannibal deities who draw Gods into themselves, be it by devouring their own children to live on within them, or in the more abstract sense employed by Aten to synchronize all the gods into his singular divinity<br /> <br /> -Unleashing: Untempered forces of their Purview at its most extreme. Generally forces of utter devastation. Surtr and Huracan are obvious examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-26-2017, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T19:32:51-07:00","id":1153363,"title":"","content":"Got it up to 10, same count as the gods. Since half though have Virtue restrictions that might make assigning 3 Callings complicated, I think going over 10 with some more without restrictions would be welcome if anyone has any thoughts, critiques, or suggestions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T20:26:03-07:00","id":1153376,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking of adding Grotesque as a Calling because specifically being a Horror to look upon and driving no others away in terror or even killing by appearance alone shows up with the Titan figures in several cultures (Izanami after she\u2019s consumed by the Death Purview, Balor, etc)<br /> <br /> 1E filled this under Epic Appearance, but since that\u2019s been replaced by the Beauty Purview, maybe being a supernatural horror in appearance, or driving people mad by the non-Euclidean geometry* of your form, etc, works as Knacks for a Titan Calling.<br /> <br /> *Anyone else always picture Lovecraft finishing a bowl of soup and screaming in horror at the sight of the concave interior of the bowl?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T20:28:36-07:00","id":1153377,"title":"","content":"Oh, this is a neat idea. There must be Warrior, and Sage echoes just like there must be a Creator echo in my mind. Balor of the Evil Eye has a martial function that is really highlighted through Cath Maige Tuired, and with his second title, &quot;Of the Mighty Blows,&quot; his strength, and physical capacity of a warrior important to his character. Similarly with Pallas, Surtr, Kingu, and Chiyou off the top of my head. The Titan-Sage would be for the All Knowing, both 'mundane' such as Prometheus and Aya (Hittite one), as well as the mystical Fate side with the Moirai, Norns, and Ishtushtaya and Papaya (Hitties).<br /> <br /> What might be a good exercise is to take a nice smattering of Titans from some Pantheons, and see if you can represent them with what you have so far here. So, for example, <b>Bres the Beautiful</b> would probably need some more support. He is most certainly Uncrowned, and <i>might</i> be a Creator if you really push your luck and use that Lugh extorted the knowledge of Agriculture from him (but this almost feels insulting to give him when other entities with Creator are people like Rhea), but nothing else quite fits. But, then again, the Irish tend to be... you know, bad at being Deities. Let's try someone else.<br /> <br /> How about... <b>Atlas</b>. (I started with Cronus, but then it gets into the argument of Cronus/=/Chronus?, Rhea, but that gets into Rhea=Cybele?, and Prometheus, but he really needs a Sage-equiv for his being as Forethought) So, he isn't an Adversary, he doesn't have a specific foe that functions on a cosmologic level. He isn't a Beast, the Greeks have a thing about that. Not a Creator. <i>Might</i> be an Embodiment as the pillar that holds up the sky? Not Entropic, Humanist, Uncrowned, Unifier, or Unleashing. I would say he isn't Sessile either since his immobility is not due to his nature, but his prison, and the moment the Titans are freed, then Atlas wouldn't have a reason to have that Calling.<br /> <br /> So, what are we missing for Bres and Atlas to shine. Bres needs a 'Social' Calling, so does Crom Cruach off the top of my head. Both entities who are loved, well, until you get to know them and then you start to see that the adoration is problematic and has gotten you to do bad things. Atlas needs almost a more broad version of Embodiment, he doesn't embody anything, but he's a piece of the cosologic framework of reality.<br /> <br /> Playing that sort of back and forth might help you round out what's missing Glamourweaver! I'm interested to see how the Titans are represented without all of the Gods callings being accessible. I also hope we see some Gods with Titan Callings. Tezcatlipoca is the leading cause for ends of the world, physically rending a lot of them. He's got more ends of the world under his belt than Apep or Surtr. Edit: And if Horror is a Titan-Virtue, then there's a lot of Deities who could do with it.<br /> <br /> I almost like the idea of a &quot;Destroyer,&quot; Calling for Gods. Tezcatlipoca, Xhuuya (on his bad days), Shiva, sort of like the opposite end to the Creator Calling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 10-26-2017, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T20:34:56-07:00","id":1153378,"title":"","content":"First of all, I love this list and the amount of work you put into it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but A. Aren't there 11 Callings for Gods? Creator Guardian Healer Hunter Judge Leader Liminal Lover Sage Trickster Warrior. And B. Wasn't the sample Beauty Purview Boon <i>about</i> looking horrifying? I wonder if like the Epic Appearance of Old, Beauty includes horrific looking as well. Or if as suggested truly horrific looking Gods/Titans are just channeling the few horrifying Beauty Boons through other Purviews, since Gods of Beauty are usually just beautiful as their thing. Gods who are supremely ugly are usually that way because they represent something <i>else</i> that is horrifying and this manifests as physical ugliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T00:15:18-07:00","id":1153414,"title":"","content":"Trying to think of how these Callings might be applied to PC's, as well.<br /> <br /> Since it seems like 2e won't limit us to solely playing on the Gods' side of things. They've confirmed that the Titans in 2nd edition won't be exclusively antagonists like they were in first edition.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of our Scions rising up to become Titan avatars, themselves. The problem is trying to imagine a way to chronicle their rise to power in a form that doesn't involve them blindly abusing their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-27-2017, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T15:00:44-07:00","id":1153594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153414#post1153414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like the idea of our Scions rising up to become Titan avatars, themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear - I don't think &quot;Titan avatars&quot; are a thing like they were in 1E. Titans are divinities that are dominated by a Purview, in lieu of being linked to humanity the same way gods are. I don't think Kronus, Crom Cruach, Asherah, etc are all going to be avatars of the same &quot;Greater Fertility Titan&quot; that manifests as a Realm ala 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T15:17:49-07:00","id":1153599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153594#post1153594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to be clear - I don't think &quot;Titan avatars&quot; are a thing like they were in 1E. Titans are divinities that are dominated by a Purview, in lieu of being linked to humanity the same way gods are. I don't think Kronus, Crom Cruach, Asherah, etc are all going to be avatars of the same &quot;Greater Fertility Titan&quot; that manifests as a Realm ala 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Either way, I'm still excited to see what comes of it.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm trying to imagine what a Titan of Magic would be like.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/adventuretimewithfinnandjake/images/a/a7/S1e20_Magic_Man_rubbing_hands_together.png/revision/latest?cb=20140329151007\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-27-2017, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T15:57:50-07:00","id":1153604,"title":"","content":"Magic doesn't appear to be a specific Purview in 2E. A lot of it is covered by PSPs (ritual soul-magic for the Netjer, rune casting fate magic for the Aesir, general Metamorphosis for a Greek witch like Circe, etc), and the rest is covered by the purviews associated with the EFFECTS of the gods' magic.<br /> <br /> Were I to write up Hecate, being a sorcery goddess (perhaps a FORMER titan, but that barrier seems crossable in either direction in 2E), I'd give her the associated Purviews Darkness, Death, Fortune, Journeys, &amp; Moon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not clear yet how mortal sorcerers work, but they are due to be explored as their own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T16:08:41-07:00","id":1153607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153604#post1153604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic doesn't appear to be a specific Purview in 2E. A lot of it is covered by PSPs (ritual soul-magic for the Netjer, rune casting fate magic for the Aesir, general Metamorphosis for a Greek witch like Circe, etc), and the rest is covered by the purviews associated with the EFFECTS of the gods' magic.<br /> <br /> Were I to write up Hecate, being a sorcery goddess (perhaps a FORMER titan, but that barrier seems crossable in either direction in 2E), I'd give her the associated Purviews Darkness, Death, Fortune, Journeys, &amp; Moon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not clear yet how mortal sorcerers work, but they are due to be explored as their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, I wasn't really happy with the 1e take on Magic, anyways. It was really difficult to come up with powers and spells that couldn't have been replicated by any of the other purviews. And the whole &quot;manipulating fate&quot; aspect was incredibly vague to begin with. There really wasn't a whole lot you could do with that concept before it started to become redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-27-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T20:02:36-07:00","id":1153650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153607#post1153607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be honest, I wasn't really happy with the 1e take on Magic, anyways. It was really difficult to come up with powers and spells that couldn't have been replicated by any of the other purviews. And the whole &quot;manipulating fate&quot; aspect was incredibly vague to begin with. There really wasn't a whole lot you could do with that concept before it started to become redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I think the new system will likely work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T20:04:44-07:00","id":1153652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153378#post1153378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">t A. Aren't there 11 Callings for Gods? Creator Guardian Healer Hunter Judge Leader Liminal Lover Sage Trickster Warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, miscounted. So should have AT LEAST one more for the Titans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And B. Wasn't the sample Beauty Purview Boon <i>about</i> looking horrifying? </div> </div> </div>Was it? I had forgotten seeing sample Beauty Boons. If so that resolves any arguable need for a Grotesque Calling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T20:17:17-07:00","id":1153654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153414#post1153414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the idea of our Scions rising up to become Titan avatars, themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note, Bai Mei (the White Eyebrow) in the Shen preview, was a Scion of Laozi who achieved apotheosis as a Titan, consumed by the Epic Dexterity (or Kung Fu in his case) Purview. He's a reason for that caveat on the Humanist Calling write-up, because he has it because of his background, not his compassion - hence his having the Yin Virtue (along with Rapacity) despite not being Pantheon-aligned.<br /> <br /> Using only the above listed Purviews, I'd give him Humanist, Sessile, and Unleashing (the idea being he's a passive Yin-consumed recluse, until the dam breaks and then he's apocalyptic kung fu devastation).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, If Sage &amp; Warrior get added to the list, he'd qualify for both of those.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T21:24:13-07:00","id":1153665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153652#post1153652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it? I had forgotten seeing sample Beauty Boons. If so that resolves any arguable need for a Grotesque Calling.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sample Beauty boon was in the Shen Preview:<br /> <br /> Visage Great And Terrible : The line between beauty and monstrosity is drawn by your hand. Your very appearance instills your enemies with the absolute terror of confronting your divinity.<br /> <br /> It also contained possibly my favourite Spoiler from any Preview... that Gods who build their Legends appropriately can channel and learn Boons from one Purview through another... Kali is given as an example of a God who has that Boon but as a Death Boon, since Kali's fearsome appearance is a result of her association with Endings and Absolute Freedom. Which is generally the case for Ugly Gods... there are many Gods of Beauty, but while there are many Ugly Gods I don't think we have much in the way of Gods of Ugliness... Mythology tends to treat Beauty as an actual Purview of Divine influence and Ugliness as a side effect of being associated with some other unsavory Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T23:03:51-07:00","id":1153682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153665#post1153665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sample Beauty boon was in the Shen Preview:<br /> <br /> Visage Great And Terrible : The line between beauty and monstrosity is drawn by your hand. Your very appearance instills your enemies with the absolute terror of confronting your divinity.<br /> <br /> It also contained possibly my favourite Spoiler from any Preview... that Gods who build their Legends appropriately can channel and learn Boons from one Purview through another... Kali is given as an example of a God who has that Boon but as a Death Boon, since Kali's fearsome appearance is a result of her association with Endings and Absolute Freedom. Which is generally the case for Ugly Gods... there are many Gods of Beauty, but while there are many Ugly Gods I don't think we have much in the way of Gods of Ugliness... Mythology tends to treat Beauty as an actual Purview of Divine influence and Ugliness as a side effect of being associated with some other unsavory Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Orcs in D&amp;D have a God of Stupidity... who appears to be their primary deity!<br /> <br /> But as for ugly deities, there are plenty who are described as being hideous. But you're right, I'm having trouble thinking of any who actually governed over ugliness itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153654#post1153654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to note, Bai Mei (the White Eyebrow) in the Shen preview, was a Scion of Laozi who achieved apotheosis as a Titan, consumed by the Epic Dexterity (or Kung Fu in his case) Purview. He's a reason for that caveat on the Humanist Calling write-up, because he has it because of his background, not his compassion - hence his having the Yin Virtue (along with Rapacity) despite not being Pantheon-aligned.<br /> <br /> Using only the above listed Purviews, I'd give him Humanist, Sessile, and Unleashing (the idea being he's a passive Yin-consumed recluse, until the dam breaks and then he's apocalyptic kung fu devastation).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, If Sage &amp; Warrior get added to the list, he'd qualify for both of those.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually be interested in seeing a game that revolved around a band of Titan sponsored Scions. I'm imagining one who's patron is Typhon, and they seek to become one with the Animal purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-28-2017, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T15:01:10-07:00","id":1153807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153665#post1153665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sample Beauty boon was in the Shen Preview:<br /> <br /> Visage Great And Terrible : The line between beauty and monstrosity is drawn by your hand. Your very appearance instills your enemies with the absolute terror of confronting your divinity.<br /> <br /> It also contained possibly my favourite Spoiler from any Preview... that Gods who build their Legends appropriately can channel and learn Boons from one Purview through another... Kali is given as an example of a God who has that Boon but as a Death Boon, since Kali's fearsome appearance is a result of her association with Endings and Absolute Freedom. Which is generally the case for Ugly Gods... there are many Gods of Beauty, but while there are many Ugly Gods I don't think we have much in the way of Gods of Ugliness... Mythology tends to treat Beauty as an actual Purview of Divine influence and Ugliness as a side effect of being associated with some other unsavory Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been thinking about this a lot, and think that the choice to represent the Deities who would have previously had Negative Epic Appearance as accessing a single Boon in the Beauty Purview through another Purview is a bit odd.<br /> <br /> Firstly, this means you can have no Titans of this concept. You can have Titans of Beauty, but you can't have Titans of being Fucking Horrific Monsters. Balor could be represented as one of these Titans, though I would more often give him War, but I can see this non-existent Nega-Beauty Purview being used for him. This option is sealed off from the official game due to regulating the Disgusting, Frightening, and Horrific to accessing this concept through other Purviews.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it's a stumbling block to players who want to play the Horrific. You will need to bind one of your other Purviews to Visage of the Great and Terrible, and, while you have to go through this hoop, the other player who is just playing the Beautiful can do exactly what you do, except they don't need to jump through this hoop. The Beautiful PC could be Ugly more easily than the character who was designed around that notion. Furthermore, we obviously don't know how this will work, if there are other Boons for being Scary or if it is limited to VotGaT, but unless the Beauty Purview has a lot of Boons for being Not-Beautiful, the players who want to play Scary are more limited. You can be Beautiful, but you can't be Scary, unless the Purview contains a lot of Scary Boons,in which case I guess the question is why don't just make it a Dual-Purview like Health was in 1e.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, just as Ugliness is often a side effect of being associated with some unsavory Purview, being Beautiful is often due to being associated with a savory Purview. The Beautiful Sun, Amaterasu, Apollo, Dazhbog, that lot, are all Beautiful due to their association with the Sun. (Technically Apollo is probably Beautiful because of his links with male youth, but you know, Greeks) The Alluring Moon Deity, Sin, Chors, Selene (technically Titan) is similar. The Sexy Sex (And Farming) Deities, Freyr, Freya, Eiru, Ishtar, Eros, Aphrodite, Dionysus, Xochiquetzal, The Morrigan. All of them could be accessing the Beauty Purview through Sun, Moon, Fertility, and probably Passion (Love) as much as The Dagda is using Visage though his own Fertility, or Hel is using it through her Death.<br /> <br /> But obviously, that's insane. Of course Apollo has Beauty, of course Ishtar has it, and Freya, and Eros, and Aphrodite. These are all the unquestionably beautiful, but, their beauty is an expression of their other Divine features. Just as much as these figures deserve to have the Beauty Purview, so does The Dagda deserve to be Comically Gross, or Hel deserves to be Disgusting, or Mictlantecuhitli deserves to be Horrifying. It's tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 10-28-2017, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T15:48:29-07:00","id":1153820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153807#post1153807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have been thinking about this a lot, and think that the choice to represent the Deities who would have previously had Negative Epic Appearance as accessing a single Boon in the Beauty Purview through another Purview is a bit odd.<br /> <br /> Firstly, this means you can have no Titans of this concept. You can have Titans of Beauty, but you can't have Titans of being Fucking Horrific Monsters. Balor could be represented as one of these Titans, though I would more often give him War, but I can see this non-existent Nega-Beauty Purview being used for him. This option is sealed off from the official game due to regulating the Disgusting, Frightening, and Horrific to accessing this concept through other Purviews.<br /> <br /> Secondly, it's a stumbling block to players who want to play the Horrific. You will need to bind one of your other Purviews to Visage of the Great and Terrible, and, while you have to go through this hoop, the other player who is just playing the Beautiful can do exactly what you do, except they don't need to jump through this hoop. The Beautiful PC could be Ugly more easily than the character who was designed around that notion. Furthermore, we obviously don't know how this will work, if there are other Boons for being Scary or if it is limited to VotGaT, but unless the Beauty Purview has a lot of Boons for being Not-Beautiful, the players who want to play Scary are more limited. You can be Beautiful, but you can't be Scary, unless the Purview contains a lot of Scary Boons,in which case I guess the question is why don't just make it a Dual-Purview like Health was in 1e.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, just as Ugliness is often a side effect of being associated with some unsavory Purview, being Beautiful is often due to being associated with a savory Purview. The Beautiful Sun, Amaterasu, Apollo, Dazhbog, that lot, are all Beautiful due to their association with the Sun. (Technically Apollo is probably Beautiful because of his links with male youth, but you know, Greeks) The Alluring Moon Deity, Sin, Chors, Selene (technically Titan) is similar. The Sexy Sex (And Farming) Deities, Freyr, Freya, Eiru, Ishtar, Eros, Aphrodite, Dionysus, Xochiquetzal, The Morrigan. All of them could be accessing the Beauty Purview through Sun, Moon, Fertility, and probably Passion (Love) as much as The Dagda is using Visage though his own Fertility, or Hel is using it through her Death.<br /> <br /> But obviously, that's insane. Of course Apollo has Beauty, of course Ishtar has it, and Freya, and Eros, and Aphrodite. These are all the unquestionably beautiful, but, their beauty is an expression of their other Divine features. Just as much as these figures deserve to have the Beauty Purview, so does The Dagda deserve to be Comically Gross, or Hel deserves to be Disgusting, or Mictlantecuhitli deserves to be Horrifying. It's tricky.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not seeing that great a problem... the sidebar just gives examples of Gods whose horrific appearance is a side effect of their other Purview associations (which is, admittedly, almost all Ugly Gods). If a Scion wants to be Ugly there's literally no reason he can't just pick up only the horrific looking Boons from Beauty and call it a day. A Scion who is only interested in elemental Fire would not pick up the Words of Fire Boon, no more than a Fertility Scion who wants to only represent growth and the harvest would pick up Mother of Pestilence. Ganesha and Lakshmi are both Prosperity Gods, but while Ganesh has the Chosen People Boon, Lakshmi doesn't, since she's not a tutelary deity on the same level as him. So too a Scion who wants to be Horrific looking simply wouldn't pick up the Boon that lets them look amazing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the idea that other Gods channel Positive Beauty Boons through other Purviews... I'm totally all for that... why <i>stop</i> there? Agni is totally channeling the lightning Boons from Sky through Fire (though not any wind or cloud based ones) since the 'flame of lightning' is a integral part of his Legend. Durga is totally channeling Passion (Attachment) through Deception since the Maya of attachment is an integral part of her Legend. It's why I loved that sidebar in the first place... building your Legend in such a way that you redefine some small part of your Purview to channel a small part of another Purview is an idea I find fascinating, and want to explore further <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T16:29:58-07:00","id":1153829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153820#post1153820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually not seeing that great a problem... the sidebar just gives examples of Gods whose horrific appearance is a side effect of their other Purview associations (which is, admittedly, almost all Ugly Gods). If a Scion wants to be Ugly there's literally no reason he can't just pick up only the horrific looking Boons from Beauty and call it a day. A Scion who is only interested in elemental Fire would not pick up the Words of Fire Boon, no more than a Fertility Scion who wants to only represent growth and the harvest would pick up Mother of Pestilence. Ganesha and Lakshmi are both Prosperity Gods, but while Ganesh has the Chosen People Boon, Lakshmi doesn't, since she's not a tutelary deity on the same level as him. So too a Scion who wants to be Horrific looking simply wouldn't pick up the Boon that lets them look amazing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the idea that other Gods channel Positive Beauty Boons through other Purviews... I'm totally all for that... why <i>stop</i> there? Agni is totally channeling the lightning Boons from Sky through Fire (though not any wind or cloud based ones) since the 'flame of lightning' is a integral part of his Legend. Durga is totally channeling Passion (Attachment) through Deception since the Maya of attachment is an integral part of her Legend. It's why I loved that sidebar in the first place... building your Legend in such a way that you redefine some small part of your Purview to channel a small part of another Purview is an idea I find fascinating, and want to explore further <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I think I didn't communicate my ideas properly. What I'm thinking is that, if the 'Beauty' Purview is going to equally support both the Horrific and the Beautiful, why not call it something like Visage, or, Epic Appearance? I'm worried that, due the name, and description of the Purview in the Shen Preview, the Purview is going to be primarily focused on Beauty rather than the other side of the coin. If the Purview was called Visage, or Epic Appearance, or the description of the Purview included the idea of being horrifying or scary, I wouldn't have this concern at all. From the vague image we have gotten so far of the Purview, I'm concerned that it isn't going to have equal support for the players who want to be Scary. And, if it <i>does</i> have equal support, then I would think that the Deities who are scary would have the Beauty Purview, it would make sense.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea that Gods can use Boons from different Purviews, it <i>really helps</i> with a lot of tricky folks just like Agni. The one I always go to is Poseidon since he doesn't actually use Earth to make Earthquakes, he uses Water. The land floats on the sea in Greek Cosmology, so, through his control of the sea, he shakes the earth. This in 1e is obviously impossible, but I <i>love</i> that it's a thing in 2e.<br /> <br /> What I meant by that section is that, the idea that the Divinely Monsterous, Scary, or Disgusting don't have the Beauty Purview themselves because they can use other Purviews to tap it since the appearance of Deities is usually a reflection of their other functions, doesn't really hold water. I meant that, if the reason that Sun Wukong doesn't have Beauty is because he is using Beasts, well, then Aphrodite could just be using her Passion, or Ishtar her Fertility, that sort of thing. I didn't mean that paragraph to be a disparaging remark to the ability to use other Purviews, but that the logic behind it gave me concerns that there would be limited support for the Horrific compared to the Beautiful if the Horrific were expected to be using other Purviews to be Scary rather than Beauty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T17:16:53-07:00","id":1153839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153829#post1153829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, I think I didn't communicate my ideas properly. What I'm thinking is that, if the 'Beauty' Purview is going to equally support both the Horrific and the Beautiful, why not call it something like Visage, or, Epic Appearance? I'm worried that, due the name, and description of the Purview in the Shen Preview, the Purview is going to be primarily focused on Beauty rather than the other side of the coin. If the Purview was called Visage, or Epic Appearance, or the description of the Purview included the idea of being horrifying or scary, I wouldn't have this concern at all. From the vague image we have gotten so far of the Purview, I'm concerned that it isn't going to have equal support for the players who want to be Scary. And, if it <i>does</i> have equal support, then I would think that the Deities who are scary would have the Beauty Purview, it would make sense.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea that Gods can use Boons from different Purviews, it <i>really helps</i> with a lot of tricky folks just like Agni. The one I always go to is Poseidon since he doesn't actually use Earth to make Earthquakes, he uses Water. The land floats on the sea in Greek Cosmology, so, through his control of the sea, he shakes the earth. This in 1e is obviously impossible, but I <i>love</i> that it's a thing in 2e.<br /> <br /> What I meant by that section is that, the idea that the Divinely Monsterous, Scary, or Disgusting don't have the Beauty Purview themselves because they can use other Purviews to tap it since the appearance of Deities is usually a reflection of their other functions, doesn't really hold water. I meant that, if the reason that Sun Wukong doesn't have Beauty is because he is using Beasts, well, then Aphrodite could just be using her Passion, or Ishtar her Fertility, that sort of thing. I didn't mean that paragraph to be a disparaging remark to the ability to use other Purviews, but that the logic behind it gave me concerns that there would be limited support for the Horrific compared to the Beautiful if the Horrific were expected to be using other Purviews to be Scary rather than Beauty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the concern, but I think that there's always going to be limited support for some aspects of Purviews... there are an infinite number of potential Boons, and only so many the devs can print. Fire has two Boons for elemental flame and only one for flames of passion, and zero for flames of lightning because there's not enough mythic figures associated with that to bother giving it a Boon. There are more Good looking Gods and Heroes in myth, so those powers are natural picks for more Boon support <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the other thing... Gods of Beauty are a thing, Gods of Ugliness are much rarer, if they exist at all (I'm sure they do, given that Humanity has made Gods for a lot of things). Not all beautiful Gods should have Beauty associated... Sarasvati doesn't, even though she is among the most beautiful of Goddesses, because whatever Beauty powers she's manifesting are probably being channeled through Artistry. Durga doesn't, even though multiple myths describe her as the <i>most</i> beautiful of all Goddeses, because she's channeling it through Deception (Durga probably channels a lot of things through Deception, given how much work she put into making the concept of Maya as broad as it is and an integral part of her Legend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), Shiva is often called 'Sundaram' meaning 'beautiful', but he totally <i>is</i> channeling that through Fertility... but Lakshmi is an actual Goddess of Beauty, for all beautiful things have their source in her, Kartikkeya is prayed to for bestowing beautiful sons, Parvati is an embodiment of the beauty of Nature and Krishna (Vishnu) is the lord of the perfected realm of Goloka where all things are eternally beautiful and pristine. All those Gods have Beauty because they are associated with Beauty as a concept, not just because they're beautiful. So if you think that some of the Gods you listed are just good looking as a representation of their connection to another Purview, then I would say that that is <i>exactly</i> what they should be doing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T17:46:45-07:00","id":1153842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153839#post1153839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the concern, but I think that there's always going to be limited support for some aspects of Purviews... there are an infinite number of potential Boons, and only so many the devs can print. Fire has two Boons for elemental flame and only one for flames of passion, and zero for flames of lightning because there's not enough mythic figures associated with that to bother giving it a Boon. There are more Good looking Gods and Heroes in myth, so those powers are natural picks for more Boon support <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the other thing... Gods of Beauty are a thing, Gods of Ugliness are much rarer, if they exist at all (I'm sure they do, given that Humanity has made Gods for a lot of things). Not all beautiful Gods should have Beauty associated... Sarasvati doesn't, even though she is among the most beautiful of Goddesses, because whatever Beauty powers she's manifesting are probably being channeled through Artistry. Durga doesn't, even though multiple myths describe her as the <i>most</i> beautiful of all Goddeses, because she's channeling it through Deception (Durga probably channels a lot of things through Deception, given how much work she put into making the concept of Maya as broad as it is and an integral part of her Legend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), Shiva is often called 'Sundaram' meaning 'beautiful', but he totally <i>is</i> channeling that through Fertility... but Lakshmi is an actual Goddess of Beauty, for all beautiful things have their source in her, Kartikkeya is prayed to for bestowing beautiful sons, Parvati is an embodiment of the beauty of Nature and Krishna (Vishnu) is the lord of the perfected realm of Goloka where all things are eternally beautiful and pristine. All those Gods have Beauty because they are associated with Beauty as a concept, not just because they're beautiful. So if you think that some of the Gods you listed are just good looking as a representation of their connection to another Purview, then I would say that that is <i>exactly</i> what they should be doing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, I didn't realize the Purview wasn't actually for the Beautiful, just those pegged as having direct influence over beauty. That's... hm. That's interesting, I think that will make Beauty one of the rarest Purviews, next to Frost and Epic Dexterity. Frost is uncommon due to, you know, geography, and Epic Dexterity for whatever reason just barely ever comes up in myths.<br /> <br /> So, Deities worshiped specifically for Beauty. Who in the Deva is worshiped specifically for influence over beauty? It's... <i>very rare</i> in a lot of cultures I can think of. There's... Aphrodite, and... Ishtar, I think. Both of those are... I would need to check the actual wording of the prayers, but I think it might be less, &quot;Make me Beautiful,&quot; and more, &quot;Have me be loved,&quot; so maybe not even them since that would be Passion. No Hittite Deities, no Irish, Norse, Haida, or Ashanti Deities. None of the major Kami either, or Slavic Deities. I think that Gods and Goddesses of Beauty are actually <i>really</i> rare, like, overwhelmingly rare.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of it being a very, very narrow Purview detached from your own appearance. Most players in my games (and myself, I'll not excuse myself from that) end up going for Epic Appearance, and if Beauty actually has nothing to do with one's own physical visage, that will be really cool. I like the idea it isn't related to your own visage, and more of your capacity of manipulating the abstract notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 10-28-2017, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T20:58:03-07:00","id":1153866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153842#post1153842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, okay, I didn't realize the Purview wasn't actually for the Beautiful, just those pegged as having direct influence over beauty. That's... hm. That's interesting, I think that will make Beauty one of the rarest Purviews, next to Frost and Epic Dexterity. Frost is uncommon due to, you know, geography, and Epic Dexterity for whatever reason just barely ever comes up in myths.<br /> <br /> So, Deities worshiped specifically for Beauty. Who in the Deva is worshiped specifically for influence over beauty? It's... <i>very rare</i> in a lot of cultures I can think of. There's... Aphrodite, and... Ishtar, I think. Both of those are... I would need to check the actual wording of the prayers, but I think it might be less, &quot;Make me Beautiful,&quot; and more, &quot;Have me be loved,&quot; so maybe not even them since that would be Passion. No Hittite Deities, no Irish, Norse, Haida, or Ashanti Deities. None of the major Kami either, or Slavic Deities. I think that Gods and Goddesses of Beauty are actually <i>really</i> rare, like, overwhelmingly rare.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of it being a very, very narrow Purview detached from your own appearance. Most players in my games (and myself, I'll not excuse myself from that) end up going for Epic Appearance, and if Beauty actually has nothing to do with one's own physical visage, that will be really cool. I like the idea it isn't related to your own visage, and more of your capacity of manipulating the abstract notion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought that the light of the sun was a result of Amaterasu's radiant beauty, and that she inspired / encouraged perfectionism in those around her.<br /> <br /> One could make a case that she's a Goddess of Beauty in that respect, even if it's not outright stated.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for there being a limited number of boons, that's not strictly the case. Sure, if you go by what's presented in the book, it may seem limiting at first. But 1E pretty much encouraged us to write up our own custom boons if we wanted to. The purviews were only limited by our imagination, and what the ST was willing to permit in their games. So if you find the boons in 2E aren't up to your expectations, you can easily add on to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-29-2017, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T22:33:03-07:00","id":1153878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153842#post1153842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, okay, I didn't realize the Purview wasn't actually for the Beautiful, just those pegged as having direct influence over beauty. That's... hm. That's interesting, I think that will make Beauty one of the rarest Purviews, next to Frost and Epic Dexterity. Frost is uncommon due to, you know, geography, and Epic Dexterity for whatever reason just barely ever comes up in myths.<br /> <br /> So, Deities worshiped specifically for Beauty. Who in the Deva is worshiped specifically for influence over beauty? It's... <i>very rare</i> in a lot of cultures I can think of. There's... Aphrodite, and... Ishtar, I think. Both of those are... I would need to check the actual wording of the prayers, but I think it might be less, &quot;Make me Beautiful,&quot; and more, &quot;Have me be loved,&quot; so maybe not even them since that would be Passion. No Hittite Deities, no Irish, Norse, Haida, or Ashanti Deities. None of the major Kami either, or Slavic Deities. I think that Gods and Goddesses of Beauty are actually <i>really</i> rare, like, overwhelmingly rare.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of it being a very, very narrow Purview detached from your own appearance. Most players in my games (and myself, I'll not excuse myself from that) end up going for Epic Appearance, and if Beauty actually has nothing to do with one's own physical visage, that will be really cool. I like the idea it isn't related to your own visage, and more of your capacity of manipulating the abstract notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the gods specifically noted for their beauty (relative to godly norms) are also associated with youth &amp; beauty as dominions, often in conflation with spring/summer or dawn.<br /> <br /> Uzume for the Kami; Aengus and Aine for the Tuatha; Baldr for the Aesir; and Xochipilli and Xochiquetzal in the Teotl all immediately spring to mind.<br /> <br /> I would hope that the Epic [Physical Attributes] along with Beauty, have Boons for empowering mortals - so for example Apollo and Artemis can bless archers via Epic Dexterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-29-2017, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T23:15:58-07:00","id":1153880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153878#post1153878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hope that the Epic [Physical Attributes] along with Beauty, have Boons for empowering mortals - so for example Apollo and Artemis can bless archers via Epic Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don't, half the Deva just lost theirs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT : And even if they don't specifically have Boons that do that, I'd like it if that was at least spelt out in the Purview descriptions as something you can Marvel and eventually create your own Boons for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 10-29-2017, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T06:50:20-07:00","id":1153914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1153125-speculating-on-titan-callings?p=1153878#post1153878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the gods specifically noted for their beauty (relative to godly norms) are also associated with youth &amp; beauty as dominions, often in conflation with spring/summer or dawn.<br /> <br /> Uzume for the Kami; Aengus and Aine for the Tuatha; Baldr for the Aesir; and Xochipilli and Xochiquetzal in the Teotl all immediately spring to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak authoritatively on the others, but I can say that Aengus and Aine are not Deities of Beauty or Youth. The idea that Aengus The Macc Oc is a Youth Deity is a misunderstanding of his epithet, &quot;The Young Son,&quot; which is a reference to how he is conceived and born in a single day. Aengus is very much presented as an adult, taking part in <i>Cath Maige Tuired</i>, as well as having his own foster-children. The idea he is a Love or Youth Deity is a Victorian imposition on him. \u00c1ine is just a regionalized Soverignty Goddess, their beauty, youth (and horrific appearance, and age) are reflections of local fertility, and part of bravery tests they impose on potential kings. The idea she is related to seasonal shift is also just a breakdown of her function as a Soverignty Goddess.<br /> <br /> There <i>are </i>individuals who I would flag as being particularly attractive, mostly individuals who are able to provoke Wasting Sickness in others, wracking other people with physical sicknesses from 'withdrawal' of their presence. However, this feels like it might be better represented by Passion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}